-- title:
--   Mod p charts of X₁(M) lie in Gauss reductions
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M \ge 5$ a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K'$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField M)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the images under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational $q$-expansion field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) of $X_1(M)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and whose image in $L$ contains $\zeta$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K'$ compatible with that of $L$; let $j' \in K'$ be nonzero (as a `Fact`) with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra, and let $t$ be an element of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC k M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) (the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ inside $k((q))$) whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15). Then two inclusions hold. First, every $z \in$ `x1FunctionFieldC k M` that is integral over the $k$-subalgebra generated by $t$ has its Laurent series in the $k$-subalgebra of $k((q))$ generated by the set of all $r$ of the form $r = \bar{x}/\bar{y}$, where $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with the reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ nonzero, $\bar{x}, \bar{y}$ denote the images of $x, y$ in $k((q))$, and there is some $b$ integral over $A[j']$ in $K'$ (an element of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K' j'`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142)) with $b \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$. Second, the same statement with $t$ replaced by $t^{-1}$ and with $b$ ranging over the elements of $K'$ integral over $A[j'^{-1}]$, i.e. over [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A K' j'`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144).
--
--   This is the ring-level, $q$-expansion form of good reduction of $X_1(M)$ at a prime $p \nmid M$: the integral closures of $k[\bar\jmath]$ and $k[\bar\jmath^{-1}]$ in the mod $p$ function field are contained in the $k$-algebras generated by Gauss reductions of the corresponding integral $j$-charts over $A$. It is used in the construction of an injective algebra map out of the base change of `chartAlgFin` realising evaluation into `x1FunctionFieldC`, and hence in the identification of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(M)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOne_chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1.lean

